# 8. Candidate Structural Pattern

[DIRECTLY FROM DATA]

The strongest computational observations are:

1. For every \(n=5,\ldots,18\), the boundary maximum is known exactly and never exceeds \(q\).
2. For \(n=19\), all 288,198 boundary candidates were exactly evaluated and none had \(b\ge6\). 
3. No actual-\(q\) obstruction tree exists anywhere in the currently available exact dataset.
4. Therefore there is currently no obstruction population from which to extract a common structural signature.

[STRUCTURAL HYPOTHESIS]

Any structural explanation of the finite boundary behavior will likely need a combination of core structure and degree-2 path distribution rather than a single scalar descriptor.

